<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:18Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>What is PHP and why did it spark a global cyber-security scramble?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3qjnwye0ep5o#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:24:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3qjnwye0ep5o--d035ec0b9f40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3qjnwye0ep5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">AI uncovered long-hidden programming flaws, triggering a rare global cyber-security response.</summary></entry><entry><title>'It's been relentless' say IT workers on frontline of PHP cyber-security scramble</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxnv025d8qpmo#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:00:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxnv025d8qpmo--6bedddec950a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxnv025d8qpmo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">IT and cyber experts have told the BBC about their struggles in the last 48 hours to update their systems.</summary></entry><entry><title>The Indian workers filming their work to train AI</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvgyml6pdm9o#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:04:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvgyml6pdm9o--8cd3bc33d6ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckvgyml6pdm9o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Indian workers are being paid to film themselves at work and the footage is used to train AI.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zuckerberg wins Meta deal to help him foot bill for possible California billionaire tax</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cky83vwnyglno#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T18:26:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cky83vwnyglno--c1ff1ed6121e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cky83vwnyglno?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The Meta boss had said he would exit the state over a wealth tax that has not yet come into force.</summary></entry><entry><title>Race to update services' computer systems after cyber-security flaw found</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9j34zgmkxx1o#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T17:12:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9j34zgmkxx1o--3c6c6b81f250.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9j34zgmkxx1o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Websites were taken offline after the developers of programming language PHP said "critical vulnerabilities" had been discovered.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zoe Kleinman: PHP is the cyber equivalent of an unexploded bomb</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw98z6qlyvg3o#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:17:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw98z6qlyvg3o--08e8546be458.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw98z6qlyvg3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">It has been a dramatic, public and global response, but the cyber event hasn't happened yet.</summary></entry><entry><title>'500 new vulnerabilities' found in government, says AI minister</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c6y8lvg2p50po#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c6y8lvg2p50po--618affb72c51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c6y8lvg2p50po?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">'500 new vulnerabilities' found in government, says AI minister</summary></entry><entry><title>UK working to identify exposure after global cyber-security warning</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmx23d0k57d3o#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:23:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmx23d0k57d3o--2a375ccbde88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmx23d0k57d3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Governments and companies are scrambling to protect their websites, as Amazon says it experienced attacks before the warning was made public.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump's green card curbs test Indian tech workers' American dream</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqj34j7dk771o#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T23:06:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqj34j7dk771o--b4c060cbae4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqj34j7dk771o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">With immigration curbs and tech firms cutting foreign hiring, US residency is becoming a distant dream for many Indians.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why is Elon Musk plotting a mega-merger of SpaceX and Tesla?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr93z1e87e0do#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T23:04:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr93z1e87e0do--8d22fc4debd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr93z1e87e0do?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Musk says there's "a lot to be gained" by combining the firms in what would be the biggest merger in history.</summary></entry><entry><title>Websites taken down worldwide as critical cyber-security update issued</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmly0lg3w5x2o#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:54:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmly0lg3w5x2o--23d28394e263.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmly0lg3w5x2o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The vulnerabilities with PHP, a programming language widely used across the internet, have been described as the most significant ever found by AI.</summary></entry><entry><title>Just Eat apologises for AI food mistakes after social media ridicule</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crz981p0klvgo#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T17:04:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crz981p0klvgo--686a391ecfec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crz981p0klvgo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">A spokesperson said it was removing inaccurate AI images and pausing the rollout of the tool.</summary></entry><entry><title>Elon Musk confirms he is considering merging Tesla and SpaceX</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyl09xjke4o#0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:42:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyl09xjke4o--3dc6f12e33fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyl09xjke4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Musk says special committees within both companies have been formed to look at a possible mega-merger.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyl#2</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyl--b40d7991507a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyl?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The next generation of chip is thinner and flexible when compared to traditional silicon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyk#2</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyk--fef1a2a6f287.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyk?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The plan for an orbiting data centre involves linking satellites around Earth.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyj#2</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyj--455cb086d724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/w3ct8jyj?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">What is a supercomputer for? How does it work? And who gets to use it? We explain all</summary></entry><entry><title>Tech Life<